ch is\n<MATH_0019>\non objects and <MATH_0020> on arrows. \nThen <MATH_0021> is fibred in groupoids. \n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nIf <MATH_0022> is an object of <MATH_0023>, write\n<MATH_0024> \nfor the category of dotted arrows for the last displayed diagram with \n<MATH_0025> given by <MATH_0026>.\nThere is a functor <MATH_0027> given by\n<MATH_0028>\non objects and <MATH_0029> on arrows. \nThis exhibits an isomorphism from <MATH_0030> to\nthe fibre category of <MATH_0031> over\n<MATH_0032>.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nThere is also a functor <MATH_0033> which is \n<MATH_0034> \non objects and <MATH_0035> on arrows. \nThis functor is fully faithful and essentially surjective, hence an\nequivalence. Details omitted.\n<STRUCT_0008>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4342cd118b4d8c0b5b5b029966402c29703531129f70558dc29aed7e5a529656", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0H1B:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:fa78466d22e6431bbc47108d22677817a985bb88a0b4cb1b9b041c7ead8472c5", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p024-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:30bc8e54273147c42f01c62d5d10acf6e5698cfcdfcc4925c7ad0d5c66d410df"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:0H1B:proof"], "policy_revision": "git:e7a1627e7bce13592b8c07d43974a815ba27c0d5", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:0H1A:proof/0001", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:0H1B:proof/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [], "unit_id": "tag:0H1B:statement"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_required_terms": {"catalog_hash": "sha256:899a668e50f3487b37dd8781e9b5a88e3e16d272ad91b4078ac6b9d847935c12", "occurrences": [{"concept": "category", "projection_end": 41, "projection_start": 33, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "category"}, {"concept": "commutative-diagram", "projection_end": 95, "projection_start": 76, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "comm